Committed as b4304064. A crates.io install now prints the commit it was published from instead of dev. Build, test, clippy and fmt all pass.

Step 0 (checked before editing build.rs): the stale-hash suspicion was right. After a fresh cargo build, yoyo --version printed 40422a76, but HEAD was dbb41933. The newest build-script output also held GIT_HASH=40422a76, so build.rs hadn't rerun after new commits. I filed that as #995 and didn't fix it here. The likely cause is rerun-if-changed=DAY_COUNT, but I haven't proven that.

Changes:
• **`build.rs:** a new helper, short_sha_from_vcs_info, reads the commit from .cargo_vcs_info.json (the file cargo publish adds to the package). It returns the first 7 characters only if they are hex, and needs no new build dependency. When GIT_HASH` isn't already set, the build uses this file first and falls back to `git` as before. The rebuild trigger for the file is only added when the file exists. A local checkout has no such file, so it behaves exactly as before.
• **tests/build_vcs_info.rs (new):** tests the real helper from `build.rs`, not a copy. The real 0.2.0 file gives `365cc12`; missing, empty, truncated, too-short, non-hex and non-ASCII inputs give nothing. I also checked the test catches a real break: with the hex check removed it failed, and it passed again once restored.
• **`src/commands_info.rs:** version_line()` now calls a formatter that takes the hash and date as arguments, so tests don't depend on the build environment. A missing part is left out instead of printed as dev. With both hash and date the line is byte-identical to before, and a test pins that exactly. These lines were the only place in src/ falling back to dev; every other caller goes through version_line().
• **`CHANGELOG.md:** one [Unreleased]` line.

One change beyond the spec: a build that has a hash but no build date (no date program, likely on Windows) used to print (HASH dev) and now prints (HASH). The commit message says so.

End-to-end check (the optional step): I packaged the crate, unpacked it in /tmp outside any git repo, and changed its recorded commit to abcdef1… so the result could only come from that file. Built from there, --version printed yoyo v0.2.0 (abcdef1 2026-10-05). My first attempt reused the repo's existing build, proved nothing, and I didn't count it.

I didn't comment on or close #994: the fix only reaches users in the next release.

