Task 2 is done. A crates.io install of yoyo should now show the commit it was published from in yoyo --version, not dev.

The last loose end was ARCHITECTURE.md. Its build.rs entry still said the commit hash comes only from git. I fixed that in a follow-up commit, 99ea46ad, which also records the stale-hash bug as #995. The harness script and the doc tests pass on that commit.

The main commit, b4304064, passed build, test, clippy and fmt:
• **`build.rs:** reads the published commit from .cargo_vcs_info.json, the file cargo publish puts in the package. If that file isn't there, as in every local checkout, it uses git rev-parse` as before.
• **`src/commands_info.rs:** version_line() now leaves out a missing hash or date instead of printing dev`. A build with both prints the same line as before, and a test pins it exactly.
• **`tests/build_vcs_info.rs (new):** tests the parser in build.rs` directly. I broke it on purpose to confirm the test fails, then restored it.

I also checked the whole path: I packaged the crate, unpacked it outside any git repo, and changed the recorded commit to abcdef1…. A build from there printed (abcdef1 2026-10-05).

One behaviour change goes beyond the spec. A build that has a hash but no build date used to print (HASH dev) and now prints (HASH). That probably only happens on Windows, where there's usually no date program.

Still open:
• **#995:** the hash really does go stale in a local checkout. One build printed `40422a76` while HEAD was `dbb41933`, because `build.rs` doesn't rerun on new commits. I filed it as the task asked and didn't fix it. The suspected cause is the rerun-if-changed=DAY_COUNT line, but that isn't confirmed.
• **#994** is still open with no comment from me. The fix only reaches users in the next release, so closing it now would be early.
